   "answer": "## Corrections from the review\n\n- **0.67 (6 mM residual):** This number is from the chosen calibration setting, not from a comparison. This session ran no comparison. The calibration fit used an intercept and no weighting. The first run gave 0.6651401 %, and the repeat run gave the same value. The table below shows the source for each residual.\n- **3.59 (3 mM residual):** The logged value is −3.5895777 %, from the same calibration fit. The first run and the repeat run both logged this value.\n\n## Results\n\n**Trace and settings (run of sample.txt)**\n\n- File: /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/data/chure2024-hplc-py/sample.txt. Detector channel: Intensity. Time unit: min.\n- Window: 10 to 20 min. Baseline: SNIP (Statistics-sensitive Nonlinear Iterative Peak-clipping). Peak width: 5 min. Prominence: 0.01. The harness used this value, not the 0.05 I passed.\n- Area: the summed fitted signal over the peak. It is not signal times time.\n\n**1. Peaks in the 10 to 20 min window: 6 peaks**\n\n| Peak | Retention time (min) | Area | Area percent |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 10.90 | 2805655.43 | 16.73 |\n| 2 | 13.17 | 5179894.75 | 30.88 |\n| 3 | 14.45 | 4163696.59 | 24.82 |\n| 4 | 15.53 | 1807420.30 | 10.78 |\n| 5 | 16.52 | 1312688.15 | 7.83 |\n| 6 | 17.29 | 1503118.99 | 8.96 |\n\nTotal area of the six peaks: 16772474.23.\n\n**2. Fitted values for peak 1 (10.90 min)**\n\n- Amplitude: 23380.46\n- Scale: 0.158762\n- Skew: 0.691800\n\n**3. Lactose calibration**\n\nEach standard has one peak at 13.56 min. I used the same settings as the run, over the whole trace.\n\n- Number of standards: 4. Range: 0.5 to 6 mM.\n- Weighting: none. Intercept: fitted. The line is not forced through zero.\n- Slope: 156586.74 area per mM.\n- Intercept: 14624.94.\n- R squared (coefficient of determination): 0.998868.\n- Estimated limit of detection (LOD): 0.3396 mM. Estimated limit of quantification (LOQ): 1.029 mM. These come from the calibration residuals and are estimates only.\n\nResiduals of each standard, from the calibration result:\n\n| Standard (mM) | Area | Residual (area) | Residual (%), logged value |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0.5 | 89667.79 | −3250.51 | −3.6250639 (shown −3.63) |\n| 1 | 184858.17 | +13646.49 | +7.382141 (shown +7.38) |\n| 3 | 467600.29 | −16784.88 | −3.5895777 (shown −3.59) |\n| 6 | 960534.29 | +6388.90 | +0.6651401 (shown +0.67) |\n\n**4. Unknown sample (lactose_mM_2)**\n\n- Area: 312048.11. Retention time: 13.56 min.\n- Concentration: 1.8994 mM, which is 1.90 mM to two decimal places.\n- The value is inside the range of the standards (0.5 to 6 mM).\n\n## What I measured and what I infer\n\n- Measured by the tools: peak areas, retention times, the fitted parameters, the calibration values, the residuals and the unknown area.\n- Inferred from the calibration line: the concentration of 1.90 mM.\n- The residuals show a pattern. The 1 mM standard sits 7.38 % above the line. The 3 mM standard sits 3.59 % below it. The unknown lies between these two standards. Its uncertainty is probably several percent. I did not measure replicates, so I cannot give a validated uncertainty.\n\n## What is uncertain\n\n1. **Prominence:** the run used 0.01, not the 0.05 I passed.\n2. **Peak width:** you said a peak is about 5 min wide at the base. In the plot, the peaks look about 0.5 to 1 min wide. A 5 min setting can change how the peaks at 13.17 and 14.45 min are split.\n3. **Calibration shape:** the four standards each have one replicate. The residuals reach 7.38 %, so linearity is not clear.\n\n## What waits for you\n\n- Confirm whether the peak width is 5 min or closer to the observed 0.5 to 1 min.\n- Confirm that prominence 0.01 is the value you want for this run.\n\nStep results that the answer does not mention, from the record:\n- n1 read_trace: sample.txt: 4801 points from 0 to 40 (step 0.00833, even spacing). Signal -544 to 75508; it starts at 0 and ends at 19.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Baseline correction: snip · Approximate peak width, in time units: 5 · Smallest peak height that counts, as a fraction of the largest peak: 0.01 · Force the calibration line through zero: false · Weighting of the calibration fit: none.",
